"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- *Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121980.*\n\n### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.beta1, 4.6.1.stable, 4.7.dev5 a8643700c\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9597) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 63.55 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nReflectionProbe ambient light blends incorrectly with sky lighting in Compatibility (it blends to pure black instead of the sky). This issue is not present in Forward+/Mobile.\n\nThe reflection probe on the left has its ambient mode set to Environment, while the one one the right uses a custom color (green).\n\nForward+ | Mobile | Compatibility\n-|-|-\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fbf49cd3-cf4c-491a-ab1e-968b40de957a\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4f76ffab-f141-467e-b8dc-ab8b49cb0fd6\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cb47e3e2-1486-43c3-a259-e14c398f8f2f\" />\n\ncc @BastiaanOlij \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a ReflectionProbe node whose edges are visible on geometry, with no other ReflectionProbes touching its edges (so that it blends with the background sky environment).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_reflection_blend_compatibility.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26843710/test_reflection_blend_compatibility.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.